# ===== pi-config: headless tweaks for cmdline.txt =====
#
# cmdline.txt lives on the BOOT partition alongside config.txt.
# Unlike config.txt, ALL parameters must be on a SINGLE LINE (no line breaks).
#
# To use: open cmdline.txt on the boot partition and ADD these parameters
# to the END of the existing line. Do NOT replace the file or start a new line.
#
# --- Quiet boot (suppress kernel messages on boot) ---
# Add this to the existing line:
#   quiet
#
# --- Full example (default Pi OS + quiet + kernel logging to serial) ---
# console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=XXXXXXXX-02 rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait quiet
#
# --- USB OTG gadget mode (Pi Zero / Zero 2 W only) ---
# Add these to the existing line (requires dtoverlay=dwc2 in config.txt):
#   modules-load=dwc2,g_ether
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Everything must be on ONE line. There are NO comments allowed inside cmdline.txt.
# - Do not remove existing parameters (especially root= and rootwait).
# - The file shown here is documentation only — it is NOT copied automatically.
